  "problem": "Simplify the sentence \"$-7$ is integer, and it is integer and negative.\"",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's rewrite the phrase \"it is integer and negative\" as the equivalent phrase \"it is integer and it is negative.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$-7$ is integer, and it is integer and it is negative.\"\n\nThen, using the associative law, we can move the comma:\n\n\"$-7$ is integer and it is integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nNow, we can simplify the phrase \"$-7$ is integer and it is integer\" to just \"$-7$ is integer.\" The sentence now reads\n\n\"$-7$ is integer, and it is negative.\"\n\nFinally, we can write the sentence more concisely as\n\n\"$-7$ is integer and negative.\"",
